1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NDAyMjE3NjcsIm5iZiI6MTc0MDIyMTQ2NywicGF0aCI6Ii8xODAwMzIvNDE1MjYwNTA2LTVkZDMxNGIxLTFmYmUtNDc5Yy05YmRhLTI1NDViZWY0YWEzMi5wbmc_.CoI5GiITw0SvZDhsphUjKwXKjONm8CvWk5UQ06Gr_Rs)\r\n> \r\n> Note that using an HTTPS request does not work; I get a TLS handshake error -9984. I assume this is because my locally running mitmproxy doesn't have a valid SSL certificate. Is it possible to ignore SSL errors for the proxy setting (for testing purposes)?\r\n\r\nI use [tinyproxy](https://tinyproxy.github.io/) to test request proxying for HTTPS and it worked well.\r\nSeems like it's only mitmproxy's problem.\r\nI use same testing project and use following auth config in tinyproxy.\r\n```\r\nBasicAuth godot p4ssw0rd\r\n```\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c7636c12-0e2d-4bd1-89e9-f56761581817)\r\nThe tinyproxy's logfile also showed that the client connected succesfully.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676189027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954110900","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101358#issuecomment-2954110900","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101358","id":2954110900,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wFCe0","user":{"login":"ItisCaleb","id":40360126,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzYwMTI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40360126?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItisCaleb","html_url":"https://github.com/ItisCaleb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItisCaleb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItisCaleb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItisCaleb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.